  "result": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented VAT calculation for the invoice system. Here's a summary of all the changes:\n\n## Summary of VAT Implementation\n\n**Invoice calculations (invoices.js)**\n- Added `lineVAT()` function that:\n  - Calculates VAT on the line amount **after discount** (not before)\n  - Rounds VAT per line (not a percentage of invoice total)\n  - Formula: VAT = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100, rounded per line\n  - Clamps result at 0\n\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n  - subtotal = sum of all line totals\n  - discount = sum of all line discounts\n  - vat = sum of all rounded line VATs (critical: not percentage of invoice)\n  - total = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**Rendering (render.js)**\n- Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to show VAT on its own line:\n  - Shows \"VAT: \u20acxxx.xx\" only if VAT > 0\n  - Places VAT line immediately before Total line\n  - Example output:\n    ```\n    DRAFT\n    Customer Name\n      5x Item @ \u20ac50.00 = \u20ac250.00\n    VAT: \u20ac50.00\n    Total: \u20ac300.00\n    ```\n\n**Test coverage**\n- 106 total tests, all passing\n- Added 14 new tests for VAT functionality:\n  - lineVAT calculation with various scenarios\n  - lineVAT with discounts\n  - lineVAT with zero amounts (clamping)\n  - invoiceTotals with VAT only\n  - invoiceTotals with VAT and discounts\n  - invoiceTotals with multiple VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n  - invoiceTotals with VAT and tier discounts\n  - Render tests updated for VAT display\n\nThe implementation ensures VAT is properly calculated per-line and rounded per-line, exactly as specified, with the invoice VAT being the sum of these rounded values rather than a percentage of the invoice total.",
